    "name": "rlr-mixcloud-title-and-tags",
    "description": "Write a Mixcloud title and choose tags for a Rhythm Lab Radio episode in Tarik's established style. Use when drafting any cloudcast.",
    "where": "Installed in both agents; used for every package draft.",
    "installed": true,
    "text": "# Rhythm Lab Radio: Mixcloud title and tags\n\nDerived from the 100 most recent cloudcasts on the `rhythmlab` Mixcloud account (Jan 2022 to the 10.24.25 episode). These are starting rules; update them when Tarik edits a draft.\n\n## Title pattern\n`RLR M.D.YY | Artist, Artist, Artist, Artist and more`\n\n- Date format is month.day.two-digit-year with dots (`10.3.25`).\n- Prefix is `RLR`. Older posts also used `RL` and `Rl`; do not copy those.\n- Separator after the date is `|` or `:`. Both appear in recent posts. Default to `|`.\n- List 4 to 6 lead artists, comma separated, then `and more` when the show has more.\n- Keep the total under 100 characters (Mixcloud's title limit as I understand it; verify on first upload).\n- Use the exact spelling and diacritics from the Paper show notes.\n\n## Choosing lead artists (starting heuristic, to be learned)\n- Pull from both hours, not just hour 1.\n- Include at least one widely recognized name and at least one newer or lesser-known artist.\n- Prefer artists the show notes give a headline \"Angle\" or a thesis role.\n- Do not pick artists whose entries carry an unresolved `VERIFY` flag if another artist works.\n- Propose two alternates. Tarik's pick teaches the agent; record which was chosen and why if he says.\n\n## Tags\n- Mixcloud shows at most 5 tags per cloudcast (72 of 100 recent posts have exactly 5).\n- Most-used tags in the archive: Jazz (84), Hip Hop (79), Electronic (74), R&B (70), Indie (41), Soul (15), Experimental (7), Afrobeats / Afropop (5).\n- Pick 5 that describe the show's two hours. Default set is Jazz, Electronic, R&B, Hip Hop, plus one of Soul or Indie.\n- Add a regional tag (Afrobeats / Afropop, Brazilian Jazz, and similar) only when a clear block of the show warrants it, and replace the weakest default tag rather than going over 5.\n\n## Never\n- Do not put release dates, \"out today\", or other time-relative phrases in a title.\n- Do not invent artists or titles not in the tracklist."
